Small change: copy `profile` into a local and use the `||` short-circuit, so `profile` is loaded once and the profile's field array is indexed once. The checks and return values are the same, so behavior does not change.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    const Profile::MESG* const p = profile;
    if (p != NULL && profileIndex < p->numFields)
        return p->fields[profileIndex].num;
    return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
}
```